Stable Ribbon Mind Map Generator

This product includes software developed from or based on:

- sawyer-shi/dify-plugins-mind_map
  Original author: sawyer-shi
  Source: https://github.com/sawyer-shi/dify-plugins-mind_map
  License: Apache License 2.0

Modifications by: Zhang Yu (GitHub: zhangyuqz)

Major modifications include:

- Report-oriented left-to-right mind map rendering.
- Style-5 ribbon-like links.
- Depth-aware node borders and rounded nodes.
- Chinese text wrapping improvements.
- Continuous-digit wrapping protection.
- Selectable PNG/lossless WebP/animated GIF output, with PNG as the default.
- Single selected-format image blob output behavior for Dify workflows.

Version 0.0.14 additions:

- Nine bundled open-source fonts and a nine-option font selector.
- Automatic multilingual rendering across 28 scripts with zero missing glyphs.
- Replaced the upstream Microsoft commercial Chinese font with
  Source Han Sans SC (SIL Open Font License).
- Pixel-budget guard for oversized documents (geometry never truncated).
- Ribbon-end visibility fixes; concurrency hardening (thread-safe canvas,
  render/transmission gates, cooperative-scheduler yield, import warm-up).

Version 0.0.16 additions:

- The bundled Han sans font is now "Ribbon Han Sans SC", a character subset
  of Source Han Sans SC (Adobe, SIL OFL 1.1) renamed per the OFL Reserved
  Font Name requirement. Copyright, trademark and license notices are
  preserved inside the font and in the bundled license file.
- Subset coverage: GB2312, high-frequency extensions, the full Japanese
  Joyo Kanji table, full Hangul syllables, full Kana and basic Cyrillic.
- Character-level fallback: Basic-plane Han characters outside the subset
  are rendered with Zhuque Fangsong automatically.

Version 0.0.22 experimental full-font and multilingual additions:

- Replaced the former character subset with Adobe's complete, unmodified
  Source Han Sans SC 2.005R Regular OTF from the official Adobe release.
- Removed the subset-only retained-character bitmap and Basic CJK fallback
  decision. All glyphs present in the official font now render directly with
  Source Han Sans SC in the default font mode.
- Preserved the other eight bundled font files and all 0.0.21 rendering,
  layout, format, and tool contracts.

Additional display-font assets included in version 0.0.22:

- Added four font-selector modes: Fusion Pixel 12px Proportional, Tiejili SC,
  Zhi Mang Xing and ZCOOL KuaiLe. Source Han Sans SC remains the default.
- The new modes select their font per covered character, then fall back per
  character to Source Han Sans SC and the established multilingual routing.
  The original modes retain their prior behavior.
- Added actual-glyph-ink containment for the four new modes so calligraphic
  overhangs remain inside rounded rectangles, circles and both ellipse
  orientations without text compression.
- Bundled the upstream font licenses and all incorporated-component notices,
  including the four notices distributed with Fusion Pixel Font.

Additional shaping assets included in version 0.0.22:

- Added Yeseva One and Bad Script as two Latin/Cyrillic display-font modes
  without changing the thirteen earlier selector values.
- Ordered all seventeen selector entries by their primary served script while
  preserving every internal value and the Source Han Sans SC default.
- Applied independent optical-size factors to Tiejili SC (1.03x), Zhi Mang Xing
  (1.20x), and ZCOOL KuaiLe (1.08x). Only selected-font runs are compensated;
  all fallback runs retain their existing sizes.
- Added complete, unmodified Noto Naskh Arabic 2.021 and Noto Sans Mongolian
  3.002 font files, with their complete SIL OFL 1.1 license texts.
- Added isolated HarfBuzz/FreeType rasterization and Unicode bidi resolution
  for real Uyghur contextual joining, Tibetan GSUB/GPOS stack positioning,
  and traditional Mongolian top-to-bottom shaping with left-to-right columns.
- Preserved traditional Mongolian FVS, MVS, NNBSP and join controls; geometry
  measurement and final drawing now share the same complex-text alpha mask.
- Kept the root rounded rectangle and the established deterministic 50/50
  non-root rounded-rectangle versus adaptive circle/ellipse decision.

Version 0.0.23 long-map clarity repair:

- Replaced the universal 8,300-pixel edge clamp with a total-pixel canvas
  budget and iterative DPI-aware layout, retaining the prior pixel envelope.
- Preserved PNG resolution before bounded RGB precision reduction and
  measured-size resampling; removed the coarse global palette fallback.
- Limited oversized WebP exports to the codec's supported dimensions.
- Released the completed Agg raster before Pillow drawing and recorded
  resolution-only diagnostics without input Markdown or personal text.
